  THE LIBRARY INDEX, MINIMAL AND TEMPORARY.

  The designed version is a separate piece of work. This exists because
  nav.footer links /library/ from every page on the site and nothing served it,
  so the footer pointed at a 404 nine times over. A minimal real page is better
  than a dead link and much better than removing the link, since the tier is
  real: src/library/ holds articles and they publish at /library/<slug>/.

  DELIBERATELY NOT A LISTING. Listing the two disposable fixtures would publish
  them as if they were writing, and ARTICLE_SYSTEM.md section 11 has them
  marked for deletion. When the designed version lands it reads
  collections.library the way the hub reads collections.yelp.

  Not in src/library/, for the same reason the hub is not in src/yelp/: that
  directory's 11tydata.js makes every file in it an article.
#}

